1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The Gentleman Bastards are masters of deception, disguise, and fine cuisine.

2
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Father Chains, their "garrista" leader, is a priest of the Crooked Warden, the god of thieves.

3
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
He buys troublesome youth Locke for his gang.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Through a series of confidence tricks on the rich, they defy the Secret Peace, an unspoken agreement between the criminal underground and the Duke's government which allows for the existence of organized crime with the understanding that the peerage and the servants of justice are off limits.

5
00:01:23,000 --> 00:02:05,000
After Chains' death, Locke becomes garrista of the group, consisting of Jean Tannen, an expert fighter; Calo and Galdo Sanza, jack-of-all-trades identical twins; Bug, a young apprentice; and Sabetha, a master charmer who resides elsewhere during the events of the novel.

6
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:23,000
The criminal underworld of Camorr is ruled with an iron fist by the Capa Barsavi, who collects a commission on all criminal activity under his purview.

7
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Under Locke's leadership, the Gentleman Bastards are known as a small gang of gentrified but petty thieves and pickpockets, and their dues, though regularly paid, are relatively small.

8
00:03:43,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Secretly, the Bastards have actually been using elaborate schemes to swindle various nobles out of large sums, and have amassed a considerable fortune; they purchase the trinkets they pass on to Barsavi as tribute, in accordance with their small-time reputation.

9
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:27,000
What little is spoken of their operations is credited to the shadowy "Thorn of Camorr."

10
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Locke pretends to be Lukas Fehrwight, a merchant from Emberlain,[3] to con Don Lorenzo Salvara and his wife.

11
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Meanwhile, a mysterious criminal calling himself the Gray King has been killing Barsavi's most trusted garristas; fearing for his safety, Barsavi has sequestered himself in his ship-fortress, the Floating Grave.

12
00:06:22,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Locke finds himself face to face with the Gray King and his hired Bondsmage "The Falconer", who somehow know what the Gentleman Bastards have been up to; Locke agrees to impersonate the Gray King in an arranged meeting with Barsavi in exchange for the Gray King's silence, as well as the Bondsmage's magical protection from Barsavi's wrath during the meeting.

13
00:07:44,000 --> 00:08:09,000
The Gray King murders Barsavi's daughter Nazca and delivers her body to the Capa in a barrel of horse urine; Locke is forced to continue with the plan, even though he knows that now Barsavi will never negotiate.

14
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:33,000
At the meeting, Barsavi manages to circumvent a disguised Locke's magical protection, having him severely beaten and left to drown in a barrel.

15
00:08:40,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Jean and Bug save him, but they realize that the Gray King has double-crossed them; they return to their secret lair and find their wealth stolen and the Sanza twins brutally murdered.

16
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:15,000
An intruder kills Bug and nearly Jean and Locke, who swear revenge.

17
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Locke goes to the Floating Grave in disguise, where Barsavi is celebrating the Gray King's supposed death.

18
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Suddenly two of Barsavi's trusted bodyguards, the fierce Berengias sisters, turn on him and cut down Barsavi and his two sons.

19
00:09:49,000 --> 00:10:07,000
The Gray King whom Locke deduces is the brother of the Berengias twins appears, introduces himself as Capa Raza and claims Barsavi's empire as his own.

20
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Left without resources and needing funds to somehow strike back at Raza, Locke tries to complete the con against the Salvaras.

21
00:10:54,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Meanwhile, Jean investigates the after-dark activity of Raza's minions and realizes that the new Capa is secretly loading his newfound wealth onto a ship supposedly quarantined for plague.

22
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Before Jean can tell Locke, he is ambushed by the Berengias sisters.

23
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,000
He manages to kill both, but is seriously wounded himself.

24
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:30,000
The Duke's "Spider", Camorr's secret spymaster who is actually the elderly Doña Vorchenza, has learned that the Salvaras are being conned by the mysterious "Thorn of Camorr."

25
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:38,000
She and the Salvaras lure Locke to the Duke's annual celebration, and he barely escapes.

26
00:12:53,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Returning to their hideout, Locke finds Jean incapacitated by the Bondsmage's sorcery, which relies on the use of Jean's true name.

27
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Locke, whose real name is not known, overpowers the Falconer and tortures him for information.

28
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Wary of revenge by other Bondsmages should he be killed, Jean and Locke remove his fingers and tongue so he cannot gesture or speak spells, leaving him alive but insane.

29
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Capa Raza has planned his revenge against Barsavi and the nobles of Camorr since childhood, when his parents were murdered as collateral damage from the Secret Peace.

30
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:39,000
To destroy the peers, he gives the Duke of Camorr four sculptures, actually time bombs filled with a substance that will cause all of the nobles and their children present at the celebration to slide into permanent mindlessness.

31
00:15:49,000 --> 00:16:04,000
Locke races back to the tower from which he escaped and manages to convince Vorchenza and the Salvaras of the danger, and the devices are defused.

32
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:15,000
He next coerces the Spider to set him free to kill Raza, and not put him on trial for theft as a reward for saving their lives.

33
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Vorchenza agrees when Locke has shared the location of the stolen money; he tells her that Raza has hidden his treasure on a waste barge, and instructs her to destroy the plague ship and its crew before Raza can use it to infect the city.

34
00:16:48,000 --> 00:17:10,000
Locke faces Raza in mortal combat even though he is outmatched by the Capa's skills with a sword, and is nearly killed before managing to distract Raza for the split second he needs to finally slay him.

35
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:37,000
When no treasure is found on the barge, Vorchenza realizes that the Thorn tricked her into destroying the ship filled with Raza's fortune, which is now an offering to the god of thieves for Locke's murdered friends.

36
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Later, Jean and Locke, recovering from their injuries, sail away to a new life.
